Wolfram wrote:
>
> I've noticed lately that people are often talking about the merits of
> having a large stack of highly enchanted daggers for missile weapons.
> The main point seems to be that you don't have to wield them to fire
> them.

That's a secondary or even tertiary point.  1) Expert
skill throws many in the same turn.  2) Unlike arrows,
daggers never disappear when they hit a monster.  3)
Unlike bows, daggers do not need to be wielded.  4)
Unlike arrows, daggers cannot be poisoned (lawfulls
vs chaotics have differing value on poison).

> But I have a question.  How many daggers are we talking about?  10...
> 50... a thousand?

The more the merrier taking weight into account.  My
characters tend to carry 10-12 daggers quivered, but
they tend to collect a lot more than that.

> And how do you go about enchanting 50 daggers to +5
> or higher?

Drop enough stuff that you can pick up your entire
stack of identically buc/enchanted/type daggers.
That is 52 blessed fireproof +2 elven daggers not
an assortment of 52 daggers.  Wield the stack (this
is why not an assortment).  Read an ?oEW.

> Don't you need _alot_ of blessed enchant weapon scrolls?

No.  One per whatever you wield.  Wield 1, enchant 1.
Wield 52, enchant 52.  Heck, with arrows wield 573,
enchant 573.

> And do you enchant normal daggers, or wait with enchanting until you
> have enough elven daggers?

That's a question of how many daggers you get of
each type and how how ?oEW you get.  On the average,
by the time you've gotten your two main weapons
highly enchanted you have collected enough elven
daggers that it is not worth enchanting lesser
dagger types.  One of the many reasons for killing
elves is they often carry elven daggers.

> In my games, as a Valkyrie, I usually collect about 5 good daggers and
> use them on neighbours, nymphs and other annoyances.  For normal
> critters I use my main weapon and I never use ?oEW on anything but
> artifacts.

Only 5 daggers?  ANY dagger is a good dagger
between the time you start the game and the time
you have cancellation to be able to merge your
huge assortment into stacks of uncursed +0
{orcish,regular,elven,silver} daggers to start
the major enchantment.  Of course, ANY dagger
isn't a good dagger for wielding purposes.

As to using which weapon when, a Valk will want
dagger at Expert ASAP but also long sword to
Skilled ASAP and also consider whatever good
artifact that shows up to Skilled ASAP.  This
means the strategy for reading scrolls is not
quite the same as the strategy for using and
enhancing.  All end up at a known place, but
the optimal order of them is an interesting
topic.



